    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d84">

                <pb facs="0174" n="76" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg76"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119/6487: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Commission to Negotiate
                            Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-09-06T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 6,
                                1919—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>3051. Your 4004, September 2d, 8 p.m. This Government is not averse on principle
                    to sign treaty on lines indicated except Government unwilling to assume any
                    positive obligations under treaty. Definite decision must await submission of
                    final draft of treaty to Department.</p>
                <p>Please forward draft in pouch.<anchor n="57" xml:id="d84-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d84-f1" n="57" xml:id="d84-f1-content">
                <p>Copies of draft treaty, in French and English, were forwarded on Sept. 12, 1919,
                    by the Commission to Negotiate Peace (file no. 763.72119/7020); not printed. For
                    final text, see <ref target="#pg78">p. 78</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
